ife in the mongolian  city of urdunet which is where his  father worked at the time it wasn't  until elementary school that zelinski  moved back to ukraine in terms of his  school life his peers say that the main  characteristics they recall about  zielinski are that he got good grades  and wore an earring moving into high  school at age 17 zielinski would join  the local kbn team which competed in  comedy tournaments each team was  required to come up with a funny  greeting improvise some jokes and  compose a humorous song that they would  perform in front of the audience and the  judges zelinski excelled in this  competition and would even be invited to  join a legacy team that would go on to  win kvn's major league in 1997. after  this victory zielinski would form his  own comedy team called the kovartal 95  that would regularly perform at the  major leagues between 1998 and 2003. in  the meantime zelinskiya also kept up  with scola as well he passed the english  language test at age 16 and would  receive an educational grant to go study  in israel but zielinski's father  insisted that he stay in ukraine so  zielinski would go on to attend kiev  national economic university where he  earned his law degree given this  traditional education you would think  that zelinski picked up a corporate job  following college but this was not the  case the comedy competitions that he was  doing on the side had garnered him a  decent amount of popularity with the  ukraine television and zielinski decided  to leverage his popularity to enter the  show business  zielinski's first career within the tv  industry outside comedy was not acting  but actually producing starting in 2003  zielinski began producing tv shows for a  ukrainian tv channel called oneplus one  the show featured the comedy team that  he founded and given their previous  popularity with kbn it didn't take long  for them to build up a loyal audience  around the same time zilinski also  dabbled with some other tv 