y  leveraged the power of social media to  run his campaign which would prove to be  extremely effective on march 31 2019 the  first round of the presidential election  was completed and zielinski would win 30  of the vote for perspective second place  only garnered 16 of the vote and just a  few weeks later on april 21st 2019 the  second round of the election would take  place and zulinski would win in a  landslide securing 73 of the vote so  zielinski hasn't even been president for  three years yet but he's already been  involved in two of the biggest political  controversies in ukraine history speak  about perfect timing  with how significant the russian  ukrainian conflict has become most of us  have completely forgotten about the  trump ukrainian drama that unfolded a  few years ago but this was quite a big  deal too as it led to the second  impeachment of donald trump the story  goes that shortly after zielinski was  elected trump called him and asked him  to investigate bain's business dealings  within ukraine which seemed reasonable  given that there seemed to be some  evidence of potential corruption the  problem though was that trump used  military aid as a bargaining chip and  refused to release 391 million dollars  worth of aid until zilinski publicly  announced a probe into buying dealings  in ukraine the military aid was supposed  to be used to strengthen ukraine's  eastern border and today it has become  painfully evident why this was so  important trump ended up releasing the  aid after his phone call with zilinski  became public but it ended up costing  him a second impeachment just as this  fiasco came to an end zelensky was hit  with another massive hurdle which was of  course the pandemic handling kovat 19  has been one of the biggest challenges  for politicians around the world from  enacting lockdowns and mass mandates to  distributing vaccines and returning to  normal life every step has been heavily  scrutinized by the media and it doesn't  help that people are heavily divided on  these subjects these issues were no  different within ukraine and  unfortunately they've experienced four  major surges since the start of the  pandemic you could say that zelinski  stood with these people during the  pandemic as well given that he caught  the illness early on before the vaccine  was approved nevertheless like the rest  of the world ukraine was just to lighten  restrictions and returned normal life as  they moved into 2022 and then the  russian invasion speculation started to  go through the roof for some reason it  looks like the lenski just can't catch a  break  by now i'm sure all of you guys know  what's going on in ukraine after weeks  of increasing pressure on ukraine by  deploying soldiers all around the  country putin decided to invade in the  last week of february at the time of  making this video no country has really  committed to helping ukraine enter the  military aid however countries and  companies from around the world have  been working together to financially and  economically punish russia this includes  loads of sanctions bans on russian  aircraft companies refusing to do  business with russia and tons of  pushback from the public while all of  these are valiant efforts in helping  ukraine in the end it's the ukrainian  people that are physically defending the  country and at the helm we have  zielinski right now it's unclear how  much longer the conflict will last and  what the result will be  there have been a few meetings between  representatives from both countries but  we are yet to receive a concrete  resolution looking forward if zilensky  and ukraine survive the conflict there's  no doubt that zielinski will be seen as  a wartime hero and he won't be leaving  the presidential position any time soon  even if things turn sour and zielinski  is captured or worse he definitely  didn't go down without a fight and i'm  sure he'd be remembered for decades to  come  for everyone's sake though hopefully we  stick with scenario number one but  that's just what i think do you guys  support zielinski and ukraine comment  that down below  also drop a like if you think zielinski  is doing a better job than lifelong  politicians and of course consider  checking out our international channels  to watch your videos in other languages  and consider subscribing to see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  you

